  "facts": [
    "The original Escambia Bay Bridge opened in 1968 as a four‑lane, no‑shoulder span, and Hurricane Ivan in 2004 ripped off 58 spans, forcing a two‑month detour via US 90.",
    "Emergency repairs finished 66 days early, earning contractors Gilbert Southern/Massman and Parsons a $1.5 million bonus each for completing the eastbound spans ahead of schedule.",
    "The new 2007 bridge added a third lane each way, shoulders, modern barriers, and lighting, and its westbound side opened December 12, 2007, after construction began in early 2006."
